<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gaius Laelius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 235–after 160 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gaius Laelius was a Roman general and statesman, the close friend and lieutenant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scipio-africanus">Publius Cornelius Scipio Africanus</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. He commanded the fleet at the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthago-nova">New Carthage</a> in 209 BCE, helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masinissa">Masinissa</a> defeat and capture <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syphax">Syphax</a> in 203 BCE and led the Roman cavalry at Zama. He was consul in 190 BCE and later a source for the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a>.</p></div>
